question:
Let \( f(x) = \begin{cases} 
      2x^2 + ax + b & \text{if } x \leq 1 \\
      3x - 2 & \text{if } x > 1 
   \end{cases}
\). Find the value of \( b \) such that \( \lim_{x \to 1} f(x) = 2 \) and \( f(x) \) is continuous at \( x = 1 \).

Find the smallest positive integer \( N \) such that:
\[
\begin{cases}
N \equiv 5 \pmod{7} \\
N \equiv 3 \pmod{11} \\
N \equiv 1 \pmod{13}
\end{cases}
\]
Compute the remainder when \( N \) is divided by \( 1001 \).

Find all positive integers \(x\) and \(y\) that satisfy the Diophantine equation:
\[ 3^x - 7^y = 2 \]
\boxed{possible_pairs}
